-- title:
--   Completed blow-up chart C[J/a] matches S[M/Ψ a]
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic and field data. Fixed are a prime $q \ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero, and an element $\xi \in L$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Further, $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2 M'$ with $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$); that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ inside $L((t))$ by the coefficientwise image of that function field.
--
--   Base ring and chart. $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-function. A uniformiser $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of $A$, and $\varpi t$ (written `ϖt`) satisfies $\varpi t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$. The chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$; $y$ is a maximal ideal of it containing $\varpi$, and `hss` asserts supersingularity at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The Drinfeld-chart witness `hArig`. This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$), every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ equal to the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin` image $z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition at $y'.asIdeal$, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\sigma\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal of $W$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)) modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ at its maximal ideal onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$. Seven compatibility clauses (summarised here) are required of these data: $e$ carries germs of constants $a \in A$ to $C(\sigma a)$; every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $L$ attached by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) to some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves the chart algebra; for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ is the identity on the chart algebra modulo $y'.asIdeal$; for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'.asIdeal$ there are $\theta \in \mathrm{Aut}(S)$, $c \in W$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $\theta$ conjugating the completed germ map by $\tau$, fixing the constants, acting on the $X_j$ by $M$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, and with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, $c \equiv 1$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, and containing tangent forms $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime $P$ of $S$ with tangent form $X_0$ the germ of a chart element lies in the contraction of $P$ exactly when all its Laurent coefficients lie in the maximal ideal of $A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and after subtraction of a suitable $a_0 \in A$ its image under $e$ is $\mathrm{mk}_S h$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0 \ge 1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form is a unit at all pairs $(a,b)$ in $W$ with one entry a unit and $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal.
--
--   The linked frame. Concretely given are a point $z$, an element $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz`, `hz` as above, a point $y'$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y : y'.asIdeal = y`; together with a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\sigma_1\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, power series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for these pinned data, exactly the same seven-clause conjunction as in the conclusion of `hArig`.
--
--   Centre, auxiliary chart and valuation subring. The ideal $J$ of the chart algebra is, by `hJ`, the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl(\Psi^{-1}\mathfrak{M}\bigr)$, where $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ over the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ that preserve the chart algebra, $\Psi = e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ is the composite of the canonical map from the chart algebra to the stalk at $z$ through $y'$, the completion map and $e_1$, and $\mathfrak{M} = (\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi t),\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1)$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is by `hB` the algebra generated over the chart algebra by all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi t \in J$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ is given with `hBW : B ⊆ W`, and: `hR1` says the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; `hR2` says $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) says $L \cap W$ is the image of $A$, the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W$ to the chart algebra, and $W$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h$ a unit of $W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) says that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation) with kernel the elements of $B$ in the maximal ideal of $W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms preserving $W$ through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained from the maximal ideal of $W$ by such an automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$ after all such translations is divisible by $\varpi$; and that an automorphism preserving $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$. Finally `hjK`, `hjC` record that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and $m \ge 1$ is a natural number with $\varpi^m = \varpi t\, w$ for a unit $w$ of $A$ (`hmt`).
--
--   The pin at the end. An element $a$ of the chart algebra is given with $a \in J$ (`haJ`) and $a \neq 0$ in $K$ (`ha0`); $B_a$ is by `hBa` the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over the chart algebra by all $x \in K$ with $xa \in J$, and $P$ is a maximal ideal of $B_a$ whose contraction to the chart algebra is $y$, in the form `hPy`: for $b$ in the chart algebra lying in $B_a$, the corresponding element of $B_a$ belongs to $P$ if and only if $b \in y$.
--
--   Conclusion. Write $\Psi = e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} : \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j \to S$ as above, $L_a =$ `Localization.Away (Ψ a)`, $\mathfrak{M} = (\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi t), \mathrm{mk}_SX_0, \mathrm{mk}_SX_1)$, and let $R \subseteq L_a$ be the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with all $x \in L_a$ such that $x \cdot \Psi a$ is the image of some $i \in \mathfrak{M}$ (the affine blow-up subring $S[\mathfrak{M}/\Psi a]$). Then $\Psi a$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$ and lies in $\mathfrak{M}$, and there exist a ring homomorphism $\Phi : B_a \to L_a$ all of whose values lie in $R$ such that: $\Phi$ agrees with $\Psi$ on the chart algebra, that is, $\Phi(c) = \Psi(c)$ in $L_a$ for every $c$ in the chart algebra that lies in $B_a$; and $\Phi(x)\cdot \Psi a = \Psi i$ in $L_a$ whenever $x \in B_a$, $i \in J$ and $xa = i$ in $K$. Moreover there exist a maximal ideal $P'$ of $R$ such that: for every $b \in B_a$ one has $\Phi b \in P'$ if and only if $b \in P$; every $s \in S$ whose image in $L_a$ lies in $R$ and which belongs to the ideal $(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi), \mathrm{mk}_SX_0, \mathrm{mk}_SX_1)$ — the $\varpi$-analogue of $\mathfrak{M}$ — has its image in $P'$; and there exists a ring isomorphism
--   $$T : \widehat{(B_a)}_P \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \widehat{R}_{P'}$$
--   between the $P$-adic completion of $B_a$ and the $P'$-adic completion of $R$ with $T(\hat b) = \widehat{\Phi b}$ for every $b \in B_a$.
--
--   This is the transfer of an affine blow-up along the chart map $\Psi$ from the supersingular chart algebra into the Drinfeld local chart $S$: it identifies the completed local ring of the blown-up chart $C[J/a]$ at a maximal ideal over $y$ with the completed local ring of the corresponding blow-up $S[\mathfrak{M}/\Psi a]$, compatibly with the map $\Phi$ extending $\Psi$. It is the middle step in the identification of the local ring at the end node of the model, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_coeff_tangent_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_coeff_tangent_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
